  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-php-2026-91767",
  "summary": "Heap-buffer-overflow in php_openssl_matches_wildcard_name on crafted server cert wildcard CN",
  "details": "php_openssl_matches_wildcard_name() in ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c underflows the length argument passed to memchr() when a TLS server certificate presents a wildcard name whose literal characters are together longer than the hostname being verified. A malicious server presenting such a certificate makes the PHP client read up to SIZE_MAX bytes past the end of a heap allocation. The path is reachable from any default client stream, because verify_peer_name is enabled by default.",
